1
00:00:14,300 --> 00:00:19,750
[NARRATOR] It was nearly two in the morning. The old city hospital was unusually quiet.

2
00:00:20,550 --> 00:00:30,930
[NARRATOR] Most of the staff had gone home, leaving behind the soft humming of machines, flickering fluorescent lights, and the distant sound of rain hitting the windows.

3
00:00:31,730 --> 00:00:41,810
[NARRATOR] Dr. John K. Smith had been working for almost twelve hours. Exhausted, he sat at his desk, finishing his coffee and preparing to leave.

4
00:00:42,610 --> 00:00:45,430
[NARRATOR] Just as he picked up his coat, the phone rang.

5
00:00:47,130 --> 00:00:53,557
[PHONE VOICE] Doctor Smith? We need you on the twelfth floor. A patient's condition is suddenly getting worse.

6
00:00:54,157 --> 00:00:55,568
[JOHN] All right, I'm coming.

7
00:00:56,368 --> 00:00:58,828
[NARRATOR] The time was 2:13 AM.

8
00:00:59,628 --> 00:01:04,428
[NARRATOR] He grabbed his stethoscope, stepped into the hallway, and headed toward the elevator.

9
00:01:05,228 --> 00:01:10,188
[NARRATOR] The hospital had twelve floors. At least, that's what everyone believed.

10
00:01:11,888 --> 00:01:15,628
[NARRATOR] John entered the elevator and pressed the button for the twelfth floor.

11
00:01:16,428 --> 00:01:19,668
[NARRATOR] The doors closed. The elevator began moving.

12
00:01:20,468 --> 00:01:24,448
[NARRATOR] Three… four… five… six…

13
00:01:25,248 --> 00:01:26,808
[NARRATOR] Everything seemed normal.

14
00:01:28,248 --> 00:01:33,768
[NARRATOR] Then the lights flickered. The elevator jerked violently, and John grabbed the handrail.

15
00:01:34,568 --> 00:01:43,348
[NARRATOR] The display continued changing. Eight… nine… ten… eleven… twelve… But the elevator didn't stop.

16
00:01:44,148 --> 00:01:51,307
[NARRATOR] John looked at the floor indicator. The number changed. … The elevator became colder.

17
00:01:47,748 --> 00:01:48,807
[JOHN] That's impossible.

18
00:01:52,107 --> 00:01:56,347
[NARRATOR] A faint sound of a child laughing echoed from somewhere inside.

19
00:01:57,447 --> 00:01:58,890
[LITTLE GIRL] Doctor...

20
00:02:00,147 --> 00:02:02,687
[NARRATOR] John turned around. Nobody was there.

21
00:02:04,187 --> 00:02:10,427
[NARRATOR] The elevator doors slowly opened. And beyond them was a corridor he had never seen before.

22
00:02:11,227 --> 00:02:14,547
[NARRATOR] A long, dark corridor stretched in front of him.

23
00:02:15,347 --> 00:02:26,827
[NARRATOR] The walls were covered in peeling paint. Dust lay across the floor. Old wheelchairs stood against the walls, and rusty hospital beds sat outside rooms with half-open doors.

24
00:02:27,627 --> 00:02:32,847
[NARRATOR] The lights flickered one after another, illuminating the corridor in brief flashes.

25
00:02:33,647 --> 00:02:40,707
[NARRATOR] John stepped out of the elevator. A sign above the hallway read: Floor 13 — Emergency Ward.

26
00:02:41,507 --> 00:02:43,756
[JOHN] This hospital doesn't have a thirteenth floor.

27
00:02:44,556 --> 00:02:50,186
[NARRATOR] He turned back toward the elevator. The doors closed. John rushed forward and pressed the button.

28
00:02:50,986 --> 00:02:54,406
[NARRATOR] Nothing happened. He pressed it again. Nothing.

29
00:02:55,206 --> 00:03:00,746
[NARRATOR] The elevator was gone. Where it had been, there was now nothing but a solid wall.

30
00:03:08,046 --> 00:03:14,246
[NARRATOR] John stepped backward, breathing faster. From somewhere down the corridor, a woman's voice called out.

31
00:03:14,646 --> 00:03:16,656
[NURSE] Doctor... (distant woman's call, Floor 13)

32
00:03:17,456 --> 00:03:21,276
[NARRATOR] John raised his flashlight and slowly walked toward the sound.

33
00:03:22,076 --> 00:03:27,296
[NARRATOR] He entered an old ward. There were ten beds. Every bed was occupied.

34
00:03:28,096 --> 00:03:31,956
[NARRATOR] The patients were lying perfectly still, facing the walls.

35
00:03:32,756 --> 00:03:34,516
[NARRATOR] John approached the first bed.

36
00:03:34,916 --> 00:03:35,669
[JOHN] Hello?

37
00:03:36,269 --> 00:03:37,141
[JOHN] Can you hear me?

38
00:03:37,941 --> 00:03:45,961
[NARRATOR] The patient slowly turned his head. His face was pale. His eyes were sunken, and his lips were almost colorless.

39
00:03:46,761 --> 00:03:48,021
[PATIENTS] You are late, Doctor.

40
00:03:49,761 --> 00:03:51,035
[JOHN] How do you know who I am?

41
00:03:52,761 --> 00:03:54,396
[PATIENTS] John K. Smith.

42
00:03:54,796 --> 00:03:56,531
[PATIENTS] We have been waiting for you.

43
00:03:57,331 --> 00:04:02,191
[NARRATOR] John moved toward the next bed. An elderly woman began laughing softly.

44
00:04:02,991 --> 00:04:05,131
[NARRATOR] Another patient whispered from the corner.

45
00:04:05,431 --> 00:04:08,952
[PATIENTS] (whisper) ...you forgot us.

46
00:04:09,752 --> 00:04:16,172
[NARRATOR] Then, one by one, all the patients turned toward him. Their heads moved at exactly the same time.

47
00:04:16,972 --> 00:04:18,072
[NARRATOR] They spoke together.

48
00:04:18,372 --> 00:04:22,788
[PATIENTS] You don't remember... but we remember you.

49
00:04:27,088 --> 00:04:28,688
[NARRATOR] John ran out of the ward.

50
00:04:30,088 --> 00:04:33,528
[NARRATOR] But as he reached the corridor, he heard a little girl's voice.

51
00:04:34,028 --> 00:04:36,542
[LITTLE GIRL] Doctor Uncle... don't leave.

52
00:04:37,342 --> 00:04:42,722
[NARRATOR] He turned. A little girl was sitting on a hospital bed, holding an old cloth doll.

53
00:04:43,522 --> 00:04:45,662
[NARRATOR] She was staring directly at him.

54
00:04:46,522 --> 00:04:47,724
[JOHN] Why are you here?

55
00:04:49,522 --> 00:04:52,064
[LITTLE GIRL] Because tonight... it's your turn.

56
00:04:56,064 --> 00:05:00,604
[NARRATOR] John hurried down the hallway until he found a door marked Medical Records.

57
00:05:01,404 --> 00:05:09,764
[NARRATOR] He pushed it open. Inside were hundreds of old files, dusty cabinets, broken chairs, and papers scattered across the floor.

58
00:05:10,564 --> 00:05:14,424
[NARRATOR] He turned on his phone's flashlight and started searching for a way out.

59
00:05:15,224 --> 00:05:21,584
[NARRATOR] Then he noticed a file lying open on a desk. The name on it made his blood run cold.

60
00:05:22,384 --> 00:05:31,964
[NARRATOR] John K. Smith. His photograph was attached to the front. His date of birth. His home address. Even his current hospital ID number.

61
00:05:32,764 --> 00:05:38,404
[NARRATOR] John opened the file with trembling hands. The first page contained a disturbing report.

62
00:05:46,204 --> 00:05:50,684
[NARRATOR] He flipped to the next page. The next page was dated eighteen years ago.

63
00:05:51,284 --> 00:05:52,566
[JOHN] This can't be happening... (script: This can't be real)

64
00:05:54,666 --> 00:06:01,366
[NARRATOR] At the bottom of the file, a final line was written in red ink: Status — never discharged.

65
00:06:05,366 --> 00:06:07,266
[NARRATOR] A voice behind him said,

66
00:06:07,866 --> 00:06:09,592
[OLD DOCTOR] Now you remember, Doctor?

67
00:06:10,392 --> 00:06:11,892
[NARRATOR] John slowly turned.

68
00:06:13,392 --> 00:06:17,852
[NARRATOR] An old man stood in the doorway, wearing a faded white doctor's coat.

69
00:06:18,652 --> 00:06:26,172
[NARRATOR] The old doctor had sunken eyes and a face covered in deep wrinkles. He looked as though he hadn't slept in decades.

70
00:06:26,972 --> 00:06:28,151
[JOHN] What is this place?

71
00:06:28,451 --> 00:06:30,155
[JOHN] Why is my name in that file?

72
00:06:30,955 --> 00:06:33,609
[OLD DOCTOR] This floor belongs to those who never left.

73
00:06:34,409 --> 00:06:37,124
[JOHN] I'm alive! I was working downstairs!

74
00:06:37,324 --> 00:06:38,494
[JOHN] I need to get out of here!

75
00:06:39,294 --> 00:06:41,417
[OLD DOCTOR] Everyone says the same thing.

76
00:06:42,294 --> 00:06:43,411
[JOHN] Where is the elevator?

77
00:06:45,294 --> 00:06:46,288
[OLD DOCTOR] Find it.

78
00:06:46,888 --> 00:06:49,405
[OLD DOCTOR] If it allows you to return, you may leave.

79
00:06:50,205 --> 00:06:51,153
[JOHN] And if it doesn't?

80
00:06:53,205 --> 00:06:55,263
[OLD DOCTOR] Then you'll be waiting for the next doctor.

81
00:06:56,563 --> 00:06:59,343
[NARRATOR] Suddenly, every light in the corridor went out.

82
00:07:00,143 --> 00:07:06,083
[NARRATOR] A red EXIT sign glowed in the darkness. And from somewhere far away, a bell rang.

83
00:07:07,983 --> 00:07:13,283
[NARRATOR] John ran. He didn't know where he was going. He only knew he had to escape.

84
00:07:14,083 --> 00:07:16,963
[NARRATOR] He opened one door — another hospital corridor.

85
00:07:17,763 --> 00:07:25,303
[NARRATOR] He opened another. The same corridor. The same wheelchairs. The same flickering lights. He ran faster.

86
00:07:26,103 --> 00:07:31,363
[NARRATOR] Then he saw the little girl standing in the middle of the hallway. She was holding her doll.

87
00:07:32,163 --> 00:07:34,756
[LITTLE GIRL] Doctor... why are you running?

88
00:07:35,556 --> 00:07:41,096
[NARRATOR] But when he passed her, he noticed something. The doll's face looked exactly like his.

89
00:07:41,896 --> 00:07:42,565
[JOHN] No...

90
00:07:44,896 --> 00:07:52,336
[NARRATOR] Behind John, every patient began appearing in the corridor. One by one. Standing silently. Watching him.

91
00:07:53,136 --> 00:07:55,376
[NARRATOR] John sprinted toward the end of the hallway.

92
00:07:56,176 --> 00:08:00,356
[NARRATOR] And there it was. An elevator. Its doors were already open.

93
00:08:01,156 --> 00:08:06,216
[NARRATOR] He jumped inside. The display flashed. The elevator suddenly began descending.

94
00:08:07,416 --> 00:08:12,808
[PA] Dr. John K. Smith... your shift is not over yet.

95
00:08:13,108 --> 00:08:15,411
[JOHN] No! Open! Please!

96
00:08:16,211 --> 00:08:19,811
[NARRATOR] Thirteen… twelve… eleven… ten…

97
00:08:24,211 --> 00:08:27,431
[NARRATOR] Finally, the elevator stopped. The doors opened.

98
00:08:28,231 --> 00:08:30,171
[NARRATOR] Morning sunlight filled the lobby.

99
00:08:31,231 --> 00:08:34,351
[NARRATOR] John stumbled out onto the floor, gasping for breath.

100
00:08:35,151 --> 00:08:36,431
[NARRATOR] It was six in the morning.

101
00:08:38,151 --> 00:08:46,231
[NARRATOR] The hospital lobby was busy again. Nurses were moving between desks, patients were waiting, and sunlight streamed through the windows.

102
00:08:47,031 --> 00:08:49,811
[NARRATOR] A nurse saw John and rushed toward him.

103
00:08:50,611 --> 00:08:55,198
[NURSE] Dr. Smith! Where have you been? We've been looking for you all night!

104
00:08:55,998 --> 00:08:57,806
[JOHN] I was on the thirteenth floor.

105
00:08:58,998 --> 00:09:00,330
[NURSE] What thirteenth floor?

106
00:09:01,998 --> 00:09:03,382
[JOHN] The elevator took me there.

107
00:09:03,682 --> 00:09:07,077
[JOHN] There were patients... an old doctor... a little girl...

108
00:09:07,877 --> 00:09:11,544
[NURSE] Doctor... this hospital has never had a thirteenth floor.

109
00:09:12,344 --> 00:09:14,118
[JOHN] I saw it. I was there.

110
00:09:24,544 --> 00:09:26,642
[NURSE] Maybe you need some rest, Doctor.

111
00:09:27,544 --> 00:09:29,932
[JOHN] Maybe... maybe I just need some rest.

112
00:09:30,732 --> 00:09:35,572
[NARRATOR] John walked away, trying to convince himself it had all been a nightmare.

113
00:09:36,372 --> 00:09:47,312
[NARRATOR] But as he passed the reception desk, an old register lying open began turning pages by itself. It stopped on a blank page. A name slowly appeared.

114
00:09:48,112 --> 00:09:55,312
[NARRATOR] Dr. John K. Smith. Floor 13. Shift: tonight — 2:13 AM.

115
00:10:01,612 --> 00:10:06,852
[NARRATOR] That same night, the hospital CCTV cameras recorded an empty reception.

116
00:10:07,652 --> 00:10:14,752
[NARRATOR] At exactly 2:13 AM, the elevator doors opened by themselves. Nobody was inside.

117
00:10:15,552 --> 00:10:19,392
[NARRATOR] The floor indicator began changing. Twelve… then…

118
00:10:20,592 --> 00:10:25,718
[PA] Dr. John K. Smith... please report to Floor 13.

119
00:10:26,518 --> 00:10:29,478
[NARRATOR] A few seconds later, the reception phone rang.

120
00:10:30,978 --> 00:10:32,726
[PHONE VOICE] Is there any doctor available?

121
00:10:33,026 --> 00:10:35,294
[PHONE VOICE] We have a new patient on the thirteenth floor.

122
00:10:36,094 --> 00:10:37,426
[NURSE] What thirteenth floor? (stands in for: What? There's no thirteenth floor.)

123
00:10:39,594 --> 00:10:41,748
[PHONE VOICE] His name is John K. Smith.

124
00:10:42,548 --> 00:10:43,828
[NARRATOR] The phone went dead.

125
00:10:45,548 --> 00:10:50,408
[NARRATOR] The elevator doors slowly closed. The display remained glowing red.

126
00:10:51,208 --> 00:10:56,008
[NARRATOR] And somewhere behind those doors… a man in a white coat was waiting.

127
00:10:58,308 --> 00:10:59,108
[NARRATOR] The end.

